// # oodar/docs — Per-Package Documentation
//
// Logline: Per-package docs for the oodar host. Six .oot
//          files cover caps, requirements, build, tests, and the
//          per-symbol coverage map.
//
// Setup: RFC-0005. Website Source: openOODA/oodar/docs/.
//        The 6 .oot files are the package manual. Each file
//        is at most 256 lines per RFC-0003.
//
// Beats:
//   1. SECURITY_MODEL.oot      — the 26-token cap system, the 4 hard rules, the 6-step cap flow.
//   2. REQUIREMENTS.oot        — how oodar maps to the 10 Requirements (5-of-10 wired: 3, 4, 5, 7, 9).
//   3. CAPABILITIES_TABLE.oot  — 20 implemented + 6 future-state cap tokens.
//   4. BUILD_AND_INSTALL.oot   — canonical `gcc oodar.c`, per-file compile, polyrepo, liboodar.a.
//   5. TESTING.oot             — the 8D Red Team matrix and the 11 tier-5 tests_challenger_*.c files + 3 lint tests.
//   6. TESTING_COVERAGE.oot    — per-symbol 8D coverage map (Beat 5 table, split from TESTING.oot for the 256-line cap).
//
import "SECURITY_MODEL.oot";
import "REQUIREMENTS.oot";
import "CAPABILITIES_TABLE.oot";
import "BUILD_AND_INSTALL.oot";
import "TESTING.oot";
import "TESTING_COVERAGE.oot";
